          "title": "You'll want to know: மாணவன்",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "மாணவன் (māṇavaṉ) — \"a student\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Sanskrit māṇava, 'a young person', with the -aṉ Tamil puts on a male — the same -aṉ as makaṉ and naṇbaṉ."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Change the ending and the person changes with it: māṇavi is a girl studying, māṇavar is said with respect or of more than one. One stem, three endings, and you already had all three."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Two: the one who teaches and the one who is taught."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "guided-production",
          "title": "Guided Practice",
          "segments": [
