        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: விருந்தாளி",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "விருந்தாளி (viruntāḷi) — \"a guest\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Take it apart and the guest is named after the meal. The first half is virundu, a feast laid on for somebody; the second is āḷi, from āḷ, 'a person'. A guest, in Tamil, is the person a feast is for — the obligation is inside the word, not added to it afterwards."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "There is an older form too, viruntiṉar, carrying the -ar you now know well. Both say the same thing: somebody has arrived, and there will be food."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "That closes the run: a teacher, a student, a doctor, a farmer, a guest."
            }
          ]
        },
